{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And it shall be for you a sign upon your hand and for a remembrance between your eyes, so that the Torah of YHWH may be in your mouth</b> — its full verse-portion is <b>\"And it shall be for you a sign upon your hand and for a remembrance between your eyes, that with a mighty hand YHWH brought you out of Egypt, so that the Torah of YHWH may be in your mouth\"</b> (Exodus 13:9, 16). Its meaning is that you shall write upon your hand and between your eyes the exodus from Egypt, and you shall remember it always, <b>so that the Torah of YHWH may be in your mouth</b> — to observe His commandments and His laws, for He is your master who redeemed you from the house of slaves."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:10.230823397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}